WRITTEN CANDIDATE v77 (unreviewed), on R5 Type II r_P=3. New tools:
- Lemma U: H has exactly one v-w edge. Every label pair is exactly one support edge, and {v,w} is not an edge of the reverse path.
- A reversal symmetry (reverse rows, swap A<->B, reverse D) maps (0,2) to (2,0).
- The D-lemma.
- T3 extended to nested walks.
Excluded sub-cases:
- (0,2) with K<t, by (L1);
- (0,2) with t<K<10, by T3+C5;
- (0,2) with 10<K<15 and one P-boundary on B, by Lemma W;
- (1,1) with K>20 and two P-boundaries on B, by Lemma U: no v-w edge is possible.
